WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 060. VALUABLE WORK CAN DISAPPEAR INTO THE WORKDAY. A name, invention note, creative draft, method, dataset, or confidential know-how record can be created, shared, overwritten, or published before anyone reviews what happened.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
CAPTURE THE ARTIFACT. WHAT · WHO · WHEN · WHERE. Use an exact-bound synthetic workday. Preserve the artifact, declared contributors, source, version, timestamp, audience, disclosure state, agreement pointer, dependencies, and uncertainty.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
ROUTE—DO NOT CLASSIFY. BRAND · INVENTION · CREATIVE · METHOD · DATA. Send a potential artifact to the right accountable review path. Keep confidential handling, preservation, correction, access limits, conflicts, and urgent human escalation visible.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
WATCH THE MAP CHANGE. CAPTURED · SHARED · PUBLIC · LOST. As a synthetic item is recorded, disclosed, overwritten, or left uncaptured, update only the declared map, provenance, exposure, dependencies, and unresolved review needs.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
BOUND THE RESULT. A ROUTE IS NOT AN IP DECISION. The demo cannot determine ownership, title, inventorship, authorship, protectability, confidentiality, trade-secret status, assignment, infringement, filing deadlines, value, or legal rights.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. CAPTURE BEFORE YOU CONCLUDE. THE WORKDAY BECOMES REVIEWABLE WHEN POTENTIAL ASSETS, CONTRIBUTORS, VERSIONS, DISCLOSURES, AGREEMENTS, AND UNCERTAINTY REACH THE RIGHT HUMAN PATH.

